3|9|Contracts|In DAEDS, who contracts directly with the owner for the coordinated design package?|The architect|Every subcontractor independently|Only the contractor|Only the structural engineer|The module describes one owner-architect contract with subconsultants engaged by the architect.
3|9|Contracts|How does DADS differ from DAEDS?|The owner has separate contracts with allied design professionals|The architect builds the project personally|There are no engineering disciplines|The design is always a competition|DADS uses separate owner contracts for design professionals.
3|10|Contracts|Does DAEDS remove each allied professional's own technical liability?|No, each retains responsibility for their discipline|Yes, all liability transfers to the owner|Yes, only the architect can be liable|No discipline has liability|The module preserves each professional's responsibility for their own services.
3|10|Specialized services|Which SPP document covers specialized architectural services?|SPP 203|SPP 202|SPP 205|SPP 207|SPP 203 sets out specialized architectural services.
3|10|Specialized services|Which is an example of a specialized architectural service?|Acoustic design|Routine tenant billing only|Licensure examination administration|Land title registration|Acoustic design requires specific design expertise under SPP 203.
3|10|Specialized services|Which is another SPP 203 specialized service?|Architectural lighting design|Contractor payroll processing|PRC registration|Occupancy permit issuance|Architectural lighting is listed among specialized services.
3|11|Specialized services|What kind of work is heritage conservation under SPP 203?|Specialized architectural service|Regular contractor labor|Tenant rent collection|Exam proctoring|Heritage work requires specialized expertise beyond the core design sequence.
3|11|Specialized services|What does forensic architecture investigate?|Building defects or failures|Only historical building styles|Only competition prizes|Only property tax bills|Forensic architectural work investigates the causes and consequences of building problems.
3|11|Supervision|Which SPP document covers full-time construction supervision?|SPP 204A|SPP 204B|SPP 201|SPP 209|SPP 204A is devoted to full-time construction supervision.
